#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:646
msgid "How access rules work"
msgstr "Cómo funcionan las reglas de acceso"

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:652
#. translators: 1: the singular space label, lowercase (e.g. space, group). 2: member label, plural, lowercase (e.g. "members").
#, php-format
msgid ""
"A rule lets more people in to this %1$s: anyone who matches it gets what it "
"grants, without being added to the %2$s list. Who else gets in is set by "
"the %1$s's visibility and join policy. Adding a role, capability, trust "
"level or membership rule to a Public %1$s switches it to Private, so that "
"the rule is what decides who gets in."
msgstr ""
"Una regla deja entrar a más personas en «%1$s»: quien la cumpla obtiene lo "
"que concede, sin añadirse a la lista de %2$s. Quién más puede entrar lo "
"determinan la visibilidad y la política de acceso de «%1$s». Si añades una "
"regla de rol, capacidad, nivel de confianza o membresía a «%1$s» con "
"visibilidad Pública, cambia la visibilidad a Privada, de modo que sea la "
"regla la que decida quién entra."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:660
#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:666
#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:670
msgid "What the person can do"
msgstr "Qué puede hacer la persona"

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:666
#. translators: %s: the owner-configured noun (space, topic, reply, member or category), sometimes with a count such as "14 spaces".
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Lets matching people in to read and report. It takes nothing away from "
"people who already get in another way, such as %s on the roster."
msgstr ""
"Permite que las personas que cumplan la regla entren a leer y denunciar. No "
"quita nada a quienes ya entran de otra forma, como los de la lista (%s)."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:670
msgid "Read, plus post, reply, vote and report. The usual choice for a paid plan."
msgstr ""
"Leer, además de publicar, responder, votar y denunciar. La opción habitual "
"para un plan de pago."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:675
#. translators: 1: member label (e.g. "Member"). 2: member label, plural (e.g. "Members").
#, fuzzy, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$s lists show a matching role - Read is listed as Viewer, Participate as "
"Member. To give one person a different role, change it on the %2$s tab; "
"that keeps it a visible, per-person decision rather than a side effect of a "
"rule."
msgstr ""
"Las listas de %2$s muestran el rol que corresponde: Leer aparece como "
"Espectador y Participar como %1$s. Para dar a una persona un rol distinto, "
"cámbialo en la pestaña «%2$s»; así sigue siendo una decisión visible e "
"individual, y no un efecto secundario de una regla."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:678
msgid "A rule can never hand out moderation."
msgstr "Una regla nunca puede conceder moderación."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:682
#. translators: 1: topic label, plural, lowercase (e.g. "topics"). 2: the singular space label the site owner configured, lowercase (e.g. space, group). 3: product name shown in wp-admin (default "Jetonomy").
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Editing, closing or pinning other people's %1$s comes from the person's "
"WordPress role - set those under %3$s - Settings - Permissions. Ordinary "
"taking part is different: being admitted to any %2$s, by a rule or by the "
"roster, carries reading, posting, replying, voting and reporting on its "
"own. That holds for roles %3$s does not map, such as the ones a course or "
